---
title: "Step 2 · Journal"
description: Read and adjust journal entries, check the decisions made in the period and book payroll.
sidebar:
  order: 9
---

## Journal

**Reconcile › Journal** lists every entry of the period. Open an entry to see its source document and why it was booked.

{% screenshot id="bookkeeping/journal-list" caption="The journal of ABC PTE. LTD., Q3 2026." /%}

Posted entries are not deleted. A correction is made by reversing the entry and entering it again; most corrections are made from the bank line, invoice or bill that produced the entry (for example **Change account…**), and the reversal is made automatically.

A free-form adjusting entry is posted from **Review › Period-end adjustments** with **Post an adjusting entry**. Each adjusting entry needs a reason, and it is listed for the reviewer under **Adjustment review**.

## Answered

**Reconcile › Answered** lists every decision a person or the AI employee made in this period. Each row shows who answered and what changed.

{% screenshot id="bookkeeping/journal-answered" caption="The Answered list: the By column shows who answered." /%}

Check each answer: the account, the tax code, which bank account a statement belongs to, duplicates, and documents dated outside the period. Open a row to see the reason and the entries it affects. If an answer is wrong, change it or withdraw it from that row; the affected entries are booked again automatically.

## Payroll entries

The payroll sheets or payslips imported under **Documents › Payroll** produce the payroll entries: salaries, employer and employee CPF, and the amounts payable. Confirm the payroll sheet for each month; then match the salary and CPF payments on the bank reconciliation page.

{% aside type="caution" %}
A salary paid to a person who is not on the payroll register is raised as a question. Add the person under **Company setup › Employees**, or ask the client who the person is.
{% /aside %}
